      "latency_ms": 2175.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 11,
      "completion_tokens": 461,
      "output": "At its most fundamental level, **water** is a chemical compound and one of the most abundant and essential substances on Earth. \n\nHere is a breakdown of what water is, looking at it through different lenses:\n\n### 1. The Chemical View\nChemically, water is represented by the formula **$\\text{H}_2\\text{O}$**. This means every single molecule of water is made up of:\n*   **Two hydrogen atoms**\n*   **One oxygen atom**\n\nThese atoms are bonded together tightly. Water is famous for being the **\"universal solvent\"** because its chemical structure allows it to dissolve more substances (like salt, sugar, and minerals) than any other liquid. \n\n### 2. The Physical View\nWater is unique because it is the only natural substance on Earth that exists abundantly in three distinct physical states depending on the temperature:\n*   **Liquid:** The water we drink, swim in, and rain from the sky.\n*   **Solid (Ice):** Frozen water, which is uniquely *less dense* as a solid than as a liquid (which is why ice floats).\n*   **Gas (Vapor/Steam):** Water in the air as humidity or invisible gas.\n\n### 3. The Ecological and Geological View\nWater covers about **71% of the Earth's surface**, mostly in oceans and seas (which hold about 96.5% of all Earth's water). It is constantly moving in a continuous cycle called the **water cycle** (or hydrologic cycle): evaporating from oceans, forming clouds, falling as rain or snow, and flowing through rivers back to the sea.\n\n### 4. The Biological View\nWater is the foundation of all known life. \n*   The human body is made up of roughly **60% water**.\n*   Cells in plants, animals, and humans require water to carry out chemical reactions, transport nutrients, regulate temperature, and flush out waste. \n*   Without water, life as we know it cannot survive.\n\n**In short:** Water is a simple molecule of hydrogen and oxygen, but it is the magical, life-giving elixir that makes our blue planet unique in the universe."
